  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Multi-device contract",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "content": "> **Derived presentation view.** Grafana is not evidence authority. The importer verifies the sealed bundle first. Provenance is limited to the selected bundle slug and checksum-manifest hash. Missing evidence stays **MISSING**.\n\nOne canonical Thread is durable in PostgreSQL. Every authenticated device owns an independent cursor, resumes by cursor, and converges on the same ordered ThreadEvent projection. The selected run controls whether the sealed multi-device gate and its requirements are PASS, FAIL, or MISSING.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Multi-device qualification",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "openpoke-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
